    "updated_at": "2020-03-17T15:23:42Z",
    "body": "We could also merge `unrestricted f*` with the `f*` and making the current finite‑only floating point types use `[Finite]` or `[EnforceRange]`.\r\n\r\nAlternatively, change the `unrestricted` keyword into the `[UnrestrictedFloat]` extended attribute.\r\n\r\nThat would fix the current issue with `unrestricted f32` and `unrestricted f64` being a parse error, preventing #856 from being built.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
